{"id":"twitter:2068469349896081663","tweet_id":"2068469349896081663","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2068469349896081663","title":"@bjornhavsvik @CanadianKobzar It's not for research. You only cite secondary sources. But it can also be a treasure trove of watching stories get shap","summary":"@bjornhavsvik @CanadianKobzar It's not for research. You only cite secondary sources. But it can also be a treasure trove of watching stories get shaped over time as a tool for research. A more interesting analysis is to look at a topic across different languages.","date":"2026-06-20","published":"2026-06-20T23:01:37+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/bjornhavsvik/status/2068466475896381511","reply_tweet_id":"2068466475896381511","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@bjornhavsvik @CanadianKobzar It&#x27;s not for research. You only cite secondary sources.<br><br>But it can also be a treasure trove of watching stories get shaped over time as a tool for research.<br><br>A more interesting analysis is to look at a topic across different languages.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2068469349896081663","display_date":"June 20, 2026 · 23:01 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
