{"id":"twitter:1970303444843102708","tweet_id":"1970303444843102708","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1970303444843102708","title":"@Kikinroks1 @SamDR @RapidResponse47 @grok Anyone involved in rioting can be charged with a crime. But you can't label a domestic organization a terror","summary":"@Kikinroks1 @SamDR @RapidResponse47 @grok Anyone involved in rioting can be charged with a crime. But you can't label a domestic organization a terrorist group for fake riots or real riots, even if the group exists or does not exist. There is literally no way to do so","date":"2025-09-23","published":"2025-09-23T01:45:22+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/Kikinroks1/status/1970299415438205189","reply_tweet_id":"1970299415438205189","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@Kikinroks1 @SamDR @RapidResponse47 @grok Anyone involved in rioting can be charged with a crime.<br><br>But you can&#x27;t label a domestic organization a terrorist group for fake riots or real riots, even if the group exists or does not exist.<br><br>There is literally no way to do so</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1970303444843102708","display_date":"September 23, 2025 · 01:45 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1970296356096090550","tweet_id":"1970296356096090550","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1970296356096090550","title":"@KeepItReal230 @RapidResponse47 Yes you can charge an individual with assault and battery. You can charge an individual for acts of terrorism. You can","summary":"@KeepItReal230 @RapidResponse47 Yes you can charge an individual with assault and battery. You can charge an individual for acts of terrorism. You can't declare a domestic group, that may have existed a decade ago, a terrorist group. Under what law?","date":"2025-09-23","published":"2025-09-23T01:17:12+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/KeepItReal230/status/1970295786148897085","reply_tweet_id":"1970295786148897085","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@KeepItReal230 @RapidResponse47 Yes you can charge an individual with assault and battery.<br><br>You can charge an individual for acts of terrorism.<br><br>You can&#x27;t declare a domestic group, that may have existed a decade ago, a terrorist group.<br><br>Under what law?</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1970296356096090550","display_date":"September 23, 2025 · 01:17 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
