{"id":"twitter:1969024944827777335","tweet_id":"1969024944827777335","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1969024944827777335","title":"@OrthodoxOrigen @Timstillherelol Diasia ,as a celebration of Zeus Meilichios, shares much with Christmas The birth of Cybele in the story of Attis was","summary":"@OrthodoxOrigen @Timstillherelol Diasia ,as a celebration of Zeus Meilichios, shares much with Christmas The birth of Cybele in the story of Attis was celebrated with a pine tree. The Tree symbolism goes back to the lost PIE religions Eostore shares much with Cybele and Attis cultural exchange happened","date":"2025-09-19","published":"2025-09-19T13:05:04+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/OrthodoxOrigen/status/1969020954203337096","reply_tweet_id":"1969020954203337096","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@OrthodoxOrigen @Timstillherelol Diasia ,as a celebration of Zeus Meilichios, shares much with Christmas<br><br>The birth of Cybele in the story of Attis was celebrated with a pine tree. The Tree symbolism goes back to the lost PIE religions<br><br>Eostore shares much with Cybele and Attis<br><br>cultural exchange happened</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1969024944827777335","display_date":"September 19, 2025 · 13:05 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
