{"id":"twitter:1968300864222982295","tweet_id":"1968300864222982295","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1968300864222982295","title":"@CathyYoung63 The people and zeitgeists that radicalize don't care about political persuasion. Anything that's devisive. People are too complex to be ","summary":"@CathyYoung63 The people and zeitgeists that radicalize don't care about political persuasion. Anything that's devisive. People are too complex to be a side. If we can focus on how online recruitment and radicalization happen, maybe some bipartisan good can come of this tragedy.","date":"2025-09-17","published":"2025-09-17T13:07:49+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/CathyYoung63/status/1967980421486178582","reply_tweet_id":"1967980421486178582","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@CathyYoung63 The people and zeitgeists that radicalize don&#x27;t care about political persuasion.<br><br>Anything that&#x27;s devisive. People are too complex to be a side. <br><br>If we can focus on how online recruitment and radicalization happen, maybe some bipartisan good can come of this tragedy.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1968300864222982295","display_date":"September 17, 2025 · 13:07 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
