{"id":"twitter:1967951988383158390","tweet_id":"1967951988383158390","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1967951988383158390","title":"Catherine, while more tolerant than other Tsars, forbade the Jews of the Pale from living in any other place in the russian empire. This created uniqu","summary":"Catherine, while more tolerant than other Tsars, forbade the Jews of the Pale from living in any other place in the russian empire. This created unique Jewish culture in modern-day Belarus and Moldova, much of Lithuania, Ukraine and east-central Poland https://t.co/FYGWBZF6ts","date":"2025-09-16","published":"2025-09-16T14:01:31+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1967951159433535963","reply_tweet_id":"1967951159433535963","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Catherine, while more tolerant than other Tsars, forbade the Jews of the Pale from living in any other place in the russian empire.<br><br>This created unique Jewish culture in modern-day Belarus and Moldova, much of Lithuania, Ukraine and east-central Poland <a href=\"https://t.co/FYGWBZF6ts\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/FYGWBZF6ts</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/7fd27ce321bdc7c230f4e216ac98351d.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1967951988383158390","display_date":"September 16, 2025 · 14:01 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/7fd27ce321bdc7c230f4e216ac98351d.jpg"]}
