{"id":"twitter:1967208799716168056","tweet_id":"1967208799716168056","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1967208799716168056","title":"Empathy is not a made up new age term. Translated in the early 1900s from the German word Einfühlung meaning \"in-feeling\" In 1920s art critics used th","summary":"Empathy is not a made up new age term. Translated in the early 1900s from the German word Einfühlung meaning \"in-feeling\" In 1920s art critics used the word. By WWII psychologists were using the word as an interpersonal skill Sympathy entered English in 16th century https://x.com/JoshuaAtLarge/status/1966857139898511771","date":"2025-09-14","published":"2025-09-14T12:48:21+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Empathy is not a made up new age term.<br><br>Translated in the early 1900s from the German word Einfühlung meaning &quot;in-feeling&quot;<br><br>In 1920s art critics used the word. <br><br>By WWII psychologists were using the word as an interpersonal skill<br><br>Sympathy entered English in 16th century <a href=\"https://x.com/JoshuaAtLarge/status/1966857139898511771\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://x.com/JoshuaAtLarge/status/1966857139898511771</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1967208799716168056","display_date":"September 14, 2025 · 12:48 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
